$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Coupling of
3,5-Dichloropyrazinones with Thiophenol Resin. 3.5-Dichloropyrazinone
(0.70 mmol, 4 equiv) and diisopropylethylamine (Hunig's base) (0.3 mL,
1.76 mol, 10 equiv) were added to a suspension of deprotected resin 12
(0.176 mmol) in THF (3 mL). The reaction mixture was shaken at RT for 12
h or irradiated at 100 °C for 30 min (hold time 2 min, maximum power 100
W). After the mixture was cooled to ambient temperature, the solvent was
filtered off via a polypropylene frit cartridge. The resin was washed as
follows: THF (5 mL x 3), THF-MeOH (1:1, v/v, 5 mL x 3), and DCM (5 mL x
3). The obtained resin-bound pyrazinone was dried under vacuum. General
Procedure for Liebeskind-Srogl Cross- Coupling Reaction of Resin-Bound
Pyrazinones. A boronic acid (0.35 mmol, 2 equiv), CuTC (0.1 g, 0.53 mmol,
3 equiv), and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.0115 g, 0.01 mmol, 6 mol %) were added to a
suspension of resin-bound pyrazinone, obtained from 0.176 mmol of
trityl-protected resin 11, in THF (3 mL). The reaction mixture was shaken
at 50 °C for 2 days. After the mixture was cooled to ambient temperature,
the solvent was filtered of with a polypropylene frit cartridge, and the
resin was washed with THF-MeOH (1:1, v/v, 5 mL x 3) and THF (5 mL x 3).
The combined filtrate was absorbed on silica gel. The residue was loaded
on a short silica gel plug and eluted with a mixture DCM-n-hexane (9:1).
The solvent was concentrated in vacuo to provide 3-arylated pyrazinones
5-Chloro-1-(4-methoxybenzyl)-3-(4-methoxyphenyl)-6-
methyl-2(1H)-pyrazinone (16). Yield: 0.023 g (35%). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ
8.45 (d, 2H, J = 9.1 Hz), 7.19 (d, 2H, J = 9.1 Hz), 6.96 (d, 2H, J = 9.1
Hz), 6.87 (d, 2H, J = 9.1 Hz), 5.35 (s, 2H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 3.80 (s, 3H),
2.48 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 161.72, 159.68, 133.91, 131.20, 129.53,
129.01, 128.73, 128.34, 127.27, 114.81 (x2), 113.87, 55.71, 48.87, 30.10,
17.40. MS (EI): m/z (%) 370 (2) [MH+], 121 (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction, Liebeskind conditions in 2nd stage, alternative
reaction conditions gave lower yield, first stage is attachment to
3-mercaptophenylpropionyl AM resin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Transition Metal-Catalyzed Orthogonal Solid-Phase Decoration of the
2(1H)-Pyrazinone Scaffold Using a Sulfur Linker
