$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Deprotection of the
(p- Methoxy)benzyl Group at Position N1 of the Pyrazinone Ring on the
Solid Support. A suspension of pyrazinone 20, obtained from 0.176 mmol of
trityl protected resin 11, in a mixture of DCM-TFA (2:1, v/v) was
irradiated at 120 °C for 40 min (hold time 2 min, maximum power 120 W).
After the mixture was cooled to ambient temperature, the solvent was
filtered off with a polypropylene frit cartridge, and the resin was
washed with DCM (5 mL x 3), MeOH (5 mL x 3), and DCM (5 mL x 3). The
resulting resin 21 was dried under vaccum. General Procedure of Chan-Lam
Coupling of Pyrazinone 21 with Boronic Acids On Solid Support. Boronic
acid (0.53 mmol, 3 equiv), Cu(OAc)2 (0.096 g, 0.53 mmol, 3 equiv),
triethylamine (0.073 mL, 0.53 mmol, 3 equiv), and pyridine (0.087 mL,
1.06 mmol, 6 equiv) were added to a suspension of resin-bound pyrazinone
21, obtained starting from 0.176 mmol of trityl-protected resin 11, in
DCM (3 mL). The reaction mixture was shaken at RT for 24 h in an ambient
atmosphere; the solvent was then filtered off with a polypropylene frit
cartridge, and the resin was washed with DCM (5 mL x 3), THF-(aq) NH3
(1:1, v/v, 5 mL x 3), THF-H2O (1:1, v/v, 5 mL x 3), THF (5 mL x 3), and
DCM (5 mL x 3). The whole procedure was repeated once. The resulting
resin-bound pyrazinone 22 was dried under vacuum.
3-Phenyl-5-chloro-1-(3-chlorophenyl)-2(1H)-pyrazinone (30), yield(28%).
mp: 114-115 °C (DCM-hexane). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.39-8.36 (m, 2H),
7.49-7.27 (m, 8H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 154.0, 153.7, 140.2, 135.7, 134.9,
131.5, 131.0, 130.1, 129.8, 128.6, 127.2, 126.8, 125.5, 124.6. HRMS (EI)
Calcd for C16H10Cl2N2O: 316.0170. Found: 316.0159.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, photochemical ((2nd stage)-120W), solid-supported
reaction, Chan-Lam coupling(3rd stage), Liebeskind conditions in 4th
stage, alternative reaction conditions shown, first stage is attachment
to 3-mercaptophenylpropionyl AM resin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
